<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Simbar-Shipak</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1025–1008 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century-bce">11th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Simbar-Shipak was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> and the founder of the Second <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sealand-dynasty">Sealand Dynasty</a>, reigning from about 1025 to 1008 BCE. Of southern origin, he took the throne after the end of the Second Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isin">Isin</a> at a time of Aramean and Sutean raids. He restored the throne of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enlil">Enlil</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ekur">Ekur</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nippur">Nippur</a> and the cult of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/utu">Shamash</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sippar">Sippar</a>, and was murdered after eighteen years.</p></div>
